# Clean README

`README.md` is the public front door. Keep it durable product facts: what the SDK is, what packages exist, how to use them, where docs live.

## Put elsewhere

| Belongs in README | Belongs in `docs/releasing.md` (or nowhere) |
| --- | --- |
| Short status + link to [providers](https://db-sdk.dev/providers) | Changesets, Version PRs, version hedges |
| Install once published (`pnpm add …`) | “Queued”, “until then”, `link:` / workspace paths |
| What the SDK is and how to use it | Package matrices, npm readiness tables |

## Do not

- Narrate the release process (“first publish is queued via Changesets…”)
- Hedge versions (“expect `0.1.0`”) — versions come from package.json / npm
- Teach temporary local consumption unless the user asked for a contributor setup section
- Dump long code samples when the site docs already cover them — link to https://db-sdk.dev/docs instead
- Dump ADR process, agent notes, or changelog drafts into the README

## Example

```markdown
<!-- Bad -->
| Package | On npm |
| --- | --- |
| … big status table … |

Firestore … First publish is queued via Changesets (expect `0.1.0`). Until then, `link:`.

<!-- Good -->
Postgres and Supabase ship today. More on the [providers](https://db-sdk.dev/providers) page.
```
